text:
For decades, successive presidential administrations have failed to enforce our immigration laws, eroding the integrity of our immigration system and fueling deep concern among Americans. In recent years, federal officials have actively undermined enforcement efforts by implementing policies that encourage mass illegal migration and blatantly disregard the laws passed by Congress. This crisis has been worsened by certain state and local actors who—empowered by the federal government’s neglect—have adopted dangerous and unlawful sanctuary policies that obstruct immigration enforcement. The American people urgently need a steadfast advocate to defend their interests against this unchecked lawlessness.

That’s where FAIR’s investigations program steps in. We are the nation’s leading immigration watchdog. Our mission is to uncover abuses of power, waste, fraud, and corruption in the immigration system through targeted research and public records requests. In particular, our work is focused on:

Exposing actions at all levels of government that undermine compliance with our immigration laws;

Uncovering conflicts of interest or unethical conduct committed by government officials with respect to immigration enforcement;

Securing the disclosure of immigration-related program information so that government actors can be scrutinized and held accountable;

Highlighting problems related to immigration enforcement so that government agencies are able to investigate and resolve them; and

Revealing improper relationships between government officials and outside groups pushing anti-border agendas that are harmful to America’s sovereignty.

We accomplish these goals by channeling our investigative work into reports, briefs, op-eds and other publications. Our investigative work product, in turn, educates government officials and the general public about the impacts of uncontrolled immigration on national security, jobs, education, health care, and the environment. On that front, we have a proven track record of driving media attention and policy changes to promote responsible immigration reform that serves American interests. We invite you to explore our investigative projects and successes here.
